   "tutor": "Here is the rule: use many with things we can count (books, cars) and much with things we cannot count (milk, money).\nRight: \"How many ducks are on the lake?\" Wrong: \"How much ducks are on the lake?\" We can count ducks, so much is wrong.\nMy example: \"The desert does not get much rain.\" We cannot count rain, so I use much.\nNow you try. Write much or many:\nHow ___ bottles are there?",
